  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Dar Mr. Fantasy**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [7]\n- **Hey Jude**: rare: 13 archived performances [7]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **deadco2024-07-11.Michael_LeBlanc** (recommended): source not stated; 21 songs; 182 min; rated 4.4/5 by 5 [1]. Said about its sound: The reviewer finds the recording muddy, flat and without highlights, comparing it to the color brown [6]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- The reviewer says the recording run involved many tapers, including some taping for the first time, and the show may never be officially released in full [4]\n- The reviewer says many better-sounding Dead recordings exist on the Internet Archive, and groups it with other Sphere recordings by Phish and the Dead [6]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **deadco2024-07-11.Michael_LeBlanc**: taped by Michael LeBlanc; transferred by Hunter S; source: ^ 1: Church Audio CA-14 (omni) Bat2b custom modification > Stereo Breakout > Rode AI Micro > iPhone 14 Pro via Apogee Meta Recorder # 2: CML's Moving Picture… [1]. Also: Source 1's iPhone recording went to WAV, then Reaper, then 24-bit FLAC; Other sources are from CML's Moving Picture Videos YouTube channel and Squirrel95's Facebook Live stream, each converted to WAV, edited in Reaper and saved as 24-bit FLAC [1]",
