      "text": "The reviewer says the recording run involved many tapers, including some taping for the first time, and the show may never be officially released in full",
      "type": "scene"
     },
     {
      "recording": "deadco2024-07-11.Michael_LeBlanc",
      "song": null,
      "song_key": null,
      "src": 6,
      "text": "The reviewer finds the recording muddy, flat and without highlights, comparing it to the color brown",
      "type": "sound"
     },
     {
      "recording": null,
      "song": null,
      "song_key": null,
      "src": 6,
      "text": "The reviewer says many better-sounding Dead recordings exist on the Internet Archive, and groups it with other Sphere recordings by Phish and the Dead",
      "type": "compare"
     },
     {
      "recording": "deadco2024-07-11.Michael_LeBlanc",
      "song": null,
      "song_key": null,
      "src": 1,
      "text": "Source 1 is a Church Audio CA-14 omni mic with a modified Bat2b, through a stereo breakout and Rode AI Micro, into an iPhone 14 Pro via Apogee Meta Recorder",
      "type": "lineage"
     },
     {
      "recording": "deadco2024-07-11.Michael_LeBlanc",
      "song": null,
      "song_key": null,
      "src": 1,
      "text": "Source 1's iPhone recording went to WAV, then Reaper, then 24-bit FLAC",
      "type": "lineage"
     },
     {
      "recording": "deadco2024-07-11.Michael_LeBlanc",
      "song": null,
      "song_key": null,
      "src": 1,
      "text": "Other sources are from CML's Moving Picture Videos YouTube channel and Squirrel95's Facebook Live stream, each converted to WAV, edited in Reaper and saved as 24-bit FLAC",
      "type": "lineage"
     }
